{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he wept.</b> Because he foresaw by the holy spirit that she would not be buried with him. Another interpretation: because he came empty-handed. He said: Eliezer, my grandfather's servant, had in his hands nose-rings and bracelets and delicacies, while I have nothing in my hands — because Eliphaz son of Esau pursued him at his father's command to kill him, and overtook him; and because Eliphaz had grown up in Isaac's lap, he held back his hands. He said to him: What shall I do about my father's command? Jacob said to him: Take what is in my hand, and the poor man is accounted as dead."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:03.212002286Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}